# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director, the opening's first line. The Director speaks a cold plain style (한다).
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:38
msgid "I decide who counts as a threat. WOLF handles the rest."
msgstr "누가 위협인지는 내가 정한다. 나머지는 WOLF가 처리한다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:40
msgid "The Director thinks WOLF is still in standby."
msgstr "소장은 WOLF가 아직 대기 상태라고 생각한다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:42
msgid ""
"Nobody gives an activation command.\n"
"WOLF wakes himself."
msgstr ""
"아무도 기동 명령을 내리지 않는다.\n"
"WOLF는 스스로 깨어난다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:44
msgid ""
"The latch breaks from the inside.\n"
"WOLF steps out under his own power."
msgstr ""
"걸쇠가 안쪽에서 부서진다.\n"
"WOLF가 제 힘으로 걸어 나온다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director to WOLF, who has woken on his own.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:47
msgid "You were in standby."
msgstr "넌 대기 상태였을 텐데."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's answer to the Director: he heard the plan and refuses it.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:50
msgid "I heard you. I won't do it."
msgstr "다 들었어. 난 안 해."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director's order after WOLF refuses.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:53
msgid "Lock down maintenance. WOLF does not leave this site."
msgstr "정비 구역을 봉쇄해. WOLF는 이 시설을 떠나지 못한다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:55
msgid "WOLF turns from the Director and heads for maintenance."
msgstr "WOLF는 소장에게서 돌아서서 정비 구역으로 향한다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. They are non-binary: no gendered words about them. No particle after the slot that changes with its last sound (slot_particles): 의 (it is %s's job).
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:59
msgid "%s keeps WOLF's systems running."
msgstr "WOLF의 시스템을 계속 돌아가게 하는 건 %s의 몫이다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. They are non-binary: no gendered words about them. No particle after the slot that changes with its last sound (slot_particles): 에게 (to %s, a fault is familiar).
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:62
msgid ""
"%s knows what a fault looks like,\n"
"and this isn't one."
msgstr ""
"고장이 어떤 모습인지, %s에게는 익숙하다.\n"
"이건 고장이 아니다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:64
msgid "I heard the Director's plan for me. I woke myself. He wants me to hunt people he calls threats."
msgstr "소장이 날 두고 세운 계획을 들었어. 난 스스로 깨어났어. 소장은 자기가 위협이라 부르는 사람들을 내가 사냥하길 원해."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer answers WOLF (their name stands over the line). No gendered forms for the speaker.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:67
msgid "Then we get through maintenance before the original logs disappear."
msgstr "그럼 원본 로그가 사라지기 전에 정비 구역을 빠져나가자."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:70
msgid "That purge takes the original program logs. Once they're gone, his word is the only record."
msgstr "저 퍼지가 원본 프로그램 로그를 지워. 그게 사라지면 소장의 말만이 유일한 기록이 돼."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's question at the coolant relay; the engineer answers with one of two choices. COOLANT FAULT is the tag painted on the relay. COOLANT FAULT is the tag painted on the relay and stays English (decision D3).
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:73
msgid "That relay's tagged COOLANT FAULT. What happens if I touch it live?"
msgstr "저 릴레이에 COOLANT FAULT 표시가 붙어 있어. 전기가 흐를 때 내가 만지면 어떻게 돼?"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the relay (a button). WOLF may quote it later.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:76
msgid "The relay may vent coolant. Your call."
msgstr "릴레이에서 냉각재가 샐 수도 있어. 판단은 네게 맡길게."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the relay (a button). WOLF may quote it later.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:79
msgid "Skip the risk talk. Go now."
msgstr "위험 얘기는 됐어. 지금 가."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:81
msgid ""
"The breaker catches.\n"
"Blue light fills the coolant relay."
msgstr ""
"차단기가 걸린다.\n"
"푸른 빛이 냉각재 릴레이를 채운다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:83
msgid "The bypass handle is stiff. Coolant hisses from the relay housing and an alarm starts to wail."
msgstr "바이패스 손잡이가 뻑뻑하다. 릴레이 하우징에서 냉각재가 쉭쉭 새어 나오고 경보가 울리기 시작한다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:85
msgid "Halfway. The hiss gets louder; the alarm keeps wailing."
msgstr "절반. 쉭쉭 소리가 커지고 경보는 계속 울린다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. Avoid a past tense with the engineer as its subject ("left"): it shows their gender in Polish and Russian. Rephrase. No particle after the slot that changes with its last sound (slot_particles): 의 (where %s's hand stopped), with no past tense about the engineer.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:88
msgid "The handle holds where %s left it. The alarm keeps going."
msgstr "손잡이는 %s의 손이 멈춘 자리에 그대로 있다. 경보는 계속 울린다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:91
msgid "Back at the last checkpoint."
msgstr "마지막 체크포인트로 돌아왔다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:93
msgid "Back at the start of this stretch."
msgstr "이 구간의 시작 지점으로 돌아왔다."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the mirror port (a button, in capitals).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:97
msgid "USE WOLF'S READOUT"
